1	// Acceptance test for the change request:
2	//   "I do not want to type one figure for an invoice. Let me list the things I am charging for.
3	//    For each one give a description, how many, and the price each. Work out the total for me."
4	//
5	// An invoice is no longer a single figure: it is a LIST of the things being charged for. Opening an
6	// invoice (invoice-open-<id>, from the project's invoice list) is a navigation to that invoice's own
7	// detail page (invoice-detail-page) — a child route, not a flag. The detail page shows the invoice's
8	// line items in a table (invoice-lineitems-table); each row (lineitem-row-<id>) gives a DESCRIPTION
9	// (lineitem-description), HOW MANY (lineitem-qty), the PRICE EACH (lineitem-unitprice) and the line's
10	// own AMOUNT (lineitem-amount), which is "how many" × "price each". The invoice's total is WORKED OUT
11	// for the user (invoice-amount) as the sum of its line amounts — never typed.
12	//
13	// A new line item is added with the line-item form (lineitem-form): a description, a quantity and a
14	// unit price (lineitem-form-description / -qty / -unitprice, submitted with lineitem-form-submit).
15	// A line item must describe a real charge — a missing description, or a quantity or price that is not
16	// more than zero, is rejected with a visible error (lineitem-form-error) and nothing is added. A
17	// valid line item joins the list, its amount is worked out, the total grows to match, and it all
18	// survives a fresh load from the server.
19	//
20	// Asserts ONLY through the UI (data-testid). Data is arranged via resetAndSeed (the app's /__test__
21	// endpoint): `clients` honours { id, name, email }, `projects` honours { id, name, clientId } and an
22	// invoice honours { id, projectId, status, lineItems } where each line item is
23	// { description, qty, unitPrice }. This change surfaces no audit records, so there is nothing to
24	// assert on the audit channel.
25	import { test, expect, type Page, type Locator } from '@playwright/test';
26	import { resetAndSeed } from '../support/seed';
